  <meiHead>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Transcription: Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Mon 159-0194-7GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/f6a886a9-d0d9-46cd-ab9c-131be8cd6f29/Mon%20159-0194-7GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum. Pitches read an octave lower than there. Pitch level: H 159's letters write the piece a fifth above the Corpus Monodicum file (e.g. "di-" m n o, the file a b c); it is given here at the manuscript's level, a fifth higher and, as for all witnesses, an octave lower than the file. A single b written before "Dif-" in the Corpus Monodicum document, without text, is left out. The turn from f. 98r to 98v before "te" is taken from the facsimile.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">F-MOf</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">H 159</idno>
            <ptr target="https://calames.abes.fr/pub/ms/D01041032"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Tonary of Saint-Bénigne, Dijon, 10th–11th century; neumes and letter notation. H 159 files this gradual under tetrardus, ff. 98r–98v (Paléographie musicale VIII, table). Images: the black-and-white facsimile in Paléographie musicale VIII (1901–05), plates 189–190; the library's own scans are at https://ged.scdi-montpellier.fr/florabium45/jsp/nodoc.jsp?NODOC=2020_DOC_MONT_MBUM_6</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Mon 159-0194-7GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/f6a886a9-d0d9-46cd-ab9c-131be8cd6f29/Mon%20159-0194-7GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum. Pitches at the manuscript's level, a fifth above that file, and an octave lower.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
  </meiHead>
